00056 // If you want to use your own demangling functionality (e.g. for another language),
00057 // define TRACY_DEMANGLE and provide your own implementation of the __tracy_demangle
00058 // function. The input parameter is a function name. The demangle function must
00059 // identify whether this name is mangled, and fail if it is not. Failure is indicated
00060 // by returning nullptr. If demangling succeeds, a pointer to the C string containing
00061 // demangled function must be returned. The demangling function is responsible for
00062 // managing memory for this string. It is expected that it will be internally reused.
00063 // When a call to ___tracy_demangle is made, previous contents of the string memory
00064 // do not need to be preserved. Function may return string of any length, but the
00065 // profiler can choose to truncate it.
00066 extern "C" const char* ___tracy_demangle( const char* mangled );
